test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T06:14:50.6188018Z             "body": "Preserves original Playwright MCP tools and adds a bounded local batch/jobs companion. Publishing remains disabled. **Draft; not release-ready.**\n\nLatest completed native77 at `1329418caf04aab783bdd56606cb7279a6df1856`: **1,906 reported test passes / 7 failures**, plus macOS actual-Codex TIMED_OUT968 and one failed Windows inherited-temp Firefox diagnostic control. [Batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39729771216):1,448/4; [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39729771276):458/3. Both workflows fail. All17 non-soak jobs conclude; optional soak skips, no reported test skips/cancellations.\n\nAll Linux batch lanes and four journal lanes pass. The strict ownership-unit contract passes all five batch lanes. Five175-file production installs,15 all-action fixtures,15 extended cancellation cases (60 scenarios) and five supervised20-run screenshot/factory fixtures pass. Linux/Windows actual Codex complete1,000 actions with zero model turns/observed owned residuals. Existing Linux resource100/600 evidence at unchanged runtime source9591621 retains partial tree FD coverage.\n\nRemaining failures: Mac SDK981 and actual-Codex968 lifecycle deadlines (known terminated/removed cleanup), Windows raw screenshot server-close/kill timeouts, Windows journal RPC watchdog and two-owner MCP connection closure, and original Windows Firefox drag/prompt/iframe failures. Iframe cause is absent from its old assertion. Legacy Windows follow-up is unexecuted. Failed input effects are never replayed. Separate inherited-temp Firefox passes5/10 then pointer timeout on sixth10/23; zero observed owned residuals does not make that control pass. Healthy later transport controls do not explain historical failures.\n\nLocal diagnostic-only follow-up retains tool response in iframe assertions, fixed journal fields for wait-cap failure and fixed parsed facts from bounded stderr tails for two-owner failure. Original errors, assertions, calls and limits remain unchanged. Existing iframe2/2 and jobs2/2 eachNode22/24 pass on Linux; these are not Windows causal fixes. Native verification of this follow-up is next.\n\nAll17 ordinary per-job logs and failed-read/retry receipts are retained under docs/evidence/worker-ci-seventyseventh-* and native77-*. No artifact downloads, authorization changes, deadline raises, force clicks, input replay, default transport/channel switch, PID-based kill authority or retrospective debt clearance. Remaining G00–G18 failures and unsupported scope are recorded in docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md and docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md. No merge or release requested.\n",
